sxml check - Check that XML documents are well-formed

Usage: sxml check [--format=FORMAT] FILE...

Checks that each FILE is a well-formed XML 1.0 document that also
conforms to Namespaces in XML 1.0. No tree is built. The supported
encodings are UTF-8, UTF-16, ISO-8859-1 and US-ASCII. The external DTD
subset and external entities are not read.

Prints nothing when every FILE is well-formed. Each problem is
reported on standard error as
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: message
With --format=json, one JSON object on standard output lists every
FILE with its "status".

Exit status: 0 when every FILE is well-formed, 1 when one is not, 3
when one cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --format=FORMAT  Report format (one of: text, json; default: text)

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to check; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml check books.xml
  sxml check --format=json books.xml broken.xml
